    "### Target Distribution — Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset contains 320 Positive and 200 Negative observations.\n",
    "\n",
    "The Positive class represents approximately 61.54% of the dataset, while the Negative class represents approximately 38.46%.\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore, the target variable is not perfectly balanced, but the class distribution does not indicate an extreme class imbalance.\n",
    "\n",
    "This distribution will be considered when selecting evaluation metrics for the machine learning models. In addition to accuracy, metrics such as precision, recall, F1-score, and ROC-AUC will be evaluated."
   ]
