    "### Categorical Feature Distribution — Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "The categorical symptom and condition features show varying distributions between their `Yes` and `No` categories.\n",
    "\n",
    "Some features are relatively balanced, such as Polyuria, Itching, and Weakness, while others are more strongly dominated by the `No` category, particularly Obesity, Genital thrush, and Irritability.\n",
    "\n",
    "These differences indicate that the categorical features do not all occur with the same frequency in the dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "However, frequency alone does not determine whether a feature is useful for prediction. A feature with relatively few `Yes` observations may still have strong predictive value if its occurrence is strongly associated with the target variable.\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore, feature–target relationships will be investigated in the next stage of the EDA."
   ]
  },
